      {
        "ballot_id": "B033",
        "laureates": [
          "Hidetoshi Katori",
          "Jun Ye"
        ],
        "citation": "For the invention and realization of optical lattice clocks."
      }
    ]
  },
  "alternatives": [
    "B019",
    "B008"
  ],
  "statement": {
    "case_for": "Optical lattice clocks are a clear experimental advance: they combine exceptional precision with reproducible methods and have enabled new tests of fundamental physics. Their development across independent groups and many years supports both the reliability and lasting value of the achievement. Katori and Ye made complementary foundational contributions, giving the case a credible attribution to two individuals.",
    "case_against": "The prize boundary needs care. The case should recognize the clock invention and its realization, without implying that every later gain in optical frequency standards belongs to these two contributions. The wider metrology community has been essential to subsequent performance and applications.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "member_id": "danielsson-ulf",
        "point": "Danielsson notes that the Nobel case depends on whether the central advance is the clock concept, its realization, or later performance gains.",
        "response": "I agree this distinction matters. I would frame the prize around the invention and realization of optical lattice clocks, where Katori's and Ye's complementary advances are central, rather than later refinements as a whole."
      },
      {
        "member_id": "lindroth-eva",
        "point": "Lindroth emphasizes that the gluon discovery's credit across PETRA experiments and their collaborations needs careful historical review.",
        "response": "That is a serious reservation for B019. Independent three-jet observations make the scientific evidence compelling, but the shortlisted case still needs a defensible account of individual contributions across the experiments. B033 has a more compact attribution, so I prefer it at this stage."
      }
    ],
    "uncertainties": [
      "The precise historical boundary between the original optical lattice clock advances and later improvements across laboratories should be established."
    ],
    "conflict_note": "None apparent from the supplied profile."
  }
}
